3. To visualize the reduction, you'll need to create a link between the source and target nodes. You can do this by adding a path element to the SVG and styling it to have a different thickness at the beginning and end.
4. To make the link thicker at the beginning and thinner at the end, you can use the `stroke-width` attribute and set it to a function that returns the value of the reduction. For example:
